# What this version improves

## 1. It skips only your own checkboxes
Instead of this broad logic:

```javascript
if (paragraphStartsWithAnchorMarker(para)) skip;
```

it now uses:

```javascript
if (firstAnchoredObjectIsOurCheckbox(para)) skip;
```

That means a paragraph starting with some unrelated anchored icon, graphic, or inline object won’t automatically be treated as already converted.

---

## 2. It tracks boxes with metadata
Each created rectangle gets:

```javascript
rect.label = "CB_BOX";
rect.insertLabel("cb-type", "checklist");
rect.insertLabel("cb-version", "1");
```

That gives you a better long-term handle for:

- updates
- cleanup
- migration to a new checkbox design
- selective replacement

---

## 3. It normalizes spacing on rerun
If a paragraph already starts with your checkbox, the script can ensure there’s exactly an appropriate thin space after it.

That helps clean up cases where someone manually edited the paragraph and left:

- a regular space
- a tab
- no space at all

---

## 4. It safely handles “other anchored object first”
If the paragraph starts with an anchored object that is **not** yours, by default it skips it:

```javascript
var SKIP_IF_OTHER_ANCHORED_OBJECT_AT_START = true;
```

That’s the right production default.

If you ever decide you want a more aggressive behavior, you can change that later.

